now runs each override through `self.substitute(...)` before converting it. The exceptions are `SetEnv` types and loads with no `conf`, which keep the raw value. I also added the `Loader.substitute` base method, which raises `NotImplementedError`, and `import inspect`.\n- **`src/tox/config/loader/ini/__init__.py`** and **`src/tox/config/loader/toml/__init__.py`**: each loader gets a `substitute` method that calls `replace` with its own reference replacer.\n- **`docs/changelog/4047.bugfix.rst`** (new): the two-line entry from the spec.\n- **`docs/reference/config.rst`**: a \"Substitutions inside an override\" subsection with `versionadded:: 4.61`, placed after \"Escaping dots in override keys\".\n\n**Wider check**\n- `tests/config` passes: 6663 passed, 2 skipped. I left out `tests/config/cli/test_argcomplete.py` because the `argcomplete` module isn't installed in `.venv`, so that file fails at import before any test runs. This is a missing dependency, not a result of these changes.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- The spec didn't give the wording for the docs note, so I wrote it myself. It says overrides use the INI `{env:VAR}` form even in TOML projects.\n- The changelog's second line is wrapped at about 130 characters, which is longer than the usual 120 limit in this repo's RST files. I didn't rewrap it.", "ttft_ms": 1385, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 53875, "uuid": "451504b6-06fa-44b1-a757-a775ae32ab07", "ttft_stream_ms": 1094, "time_to_request_ms": 243, "first_content_frame_ms": 1094, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
